Before you read on

This is not an open source license. You can read the source, and you can use and
share the Work, but only in the ways set out below, and those ways are narrow on
purpose. If you want to do something this license does not mention, assume you
need to ask first.

If you do not agree to these terms, do not use the Work, and delete any copy you
have. By using, copying, or sharing the Work in any way, you agree to everything
in this document.


1. Words used in this license

"Work" means everything this license is attached to or that points to this
license: the code, the programs built from it, models and model weights, prompts,
data files, art, text, documentation, and anything else included. It also
includes any piece of it, big or small.

"We", "us", and "the Licensor" mean Canyon Lake Labs, the owner named in the
copyright line at the top.

"You" means whoever is using the Work. If you are using it for a company, school,
club, or any other group, "you" includes that group, and you promise you have the
right to speak for it.

"Share" means to hand the Work to anyone else in any way at all. Posting it,
sending it, uploading it, putting it on a drive someone else can reach, burning
it to a disc, or linking to a copy you made all count, whether you charge for it
or not.

"Changed version" means anything made by editing, adapting, translating,
rewriting, porting, merging, or building on the Work or a piece of it. Training
a model on it, tuning a model with it, or compressing or converting a model that
is part of it also counts. A changed version is treated as part of the Work for
every rule in this license.

"Bundle" means any bigger project, product, or package that contains the Work or
a changed version.

"Network use" means letting other people use the Work, or a program that
contains it, over a network, even though you never hand them a copy. A website,
an app backend, a game server, a bot, a paid or free online service, and an API
are all examples.

"Complete source" means the full, readable source of the Work exactly as you got
it, along with anything needed to build it and a copy of this license.

"Commercial use" means using the Work mainly to make money or gain a business
advantage, directly or indirectly. This covers using it for an employer, a
client, or a customer, selling it or anything that includes it, running it
behind ads, sponsorships, or affiliate links, putting it in a paid product or an
app store listing, and any use inside a business. Passing it around for free
among regular people who are not paying or being paid does not make it
commercial.

"AI use" means using the Work, or any piece of it, to train, tune, test,
benchmark, rank, or improve any machine learning model or other automated
system. It also means feeding the Work into a search index, an embedding
database, a retrieval system, a dataset, or a chatbot that is meant to learn
from it, and it means having any bot or crawler gather the Work for any of
these reasons.


2. What you are allowed to do

If you follow every rule in this license, you may:

(a) Use the Work. You can run it, read it, and study how it works, for your own
    personal, non-commercial purposes. Hobby projects, learning, and tinkering
    at home are fine.

(b) Share the Work as it is. You can copy it and pass it on to other people, in
    any format, as long as you do not charge for it, you do not get anything in
    return for it, and every condition in section 3 is met. The copy you share
    has to be exactly the copy you received.

(c) Change it for yourself. You can make a changed version for your own private
    use. It stays on your own devices. You cannot share it, post it, host it, or
    let other people use it over a network, not even to a friend. Not even a
    patch, a diff, a screenshot of the code, or a description detailed enough to
    recreate the changes.

Nothing in this list gives you more than it says. Anything not listed is not
allowed unless we agree in writing.


3. Rules for sharing the Work

If you share the Work, all of these things must be true.

You keep the credit. Leave every copyright notice, author credit, and license
notice where it is. Tell people the Work comes from Canyon Lake Labs, give them
the full text of this license or a working link to it, and say that the Work is
under the Canyon Lake Labs License version 1.0. Do not say or imply that we
support you, your project, or how you are using the Work.

The license stays. Every copy you hand over has to include this license, word for
word. You cannot swap it for another license, add a second license beside it,
offer a paid "business version", or change any term. People who get the Work from
you receive their permission straight from us, under this license and nothing
else.

It stays unchanged. What you share has to match what you received, exactly. You
may add a separate file with the credits that section 3 asks for, but you may not
edit the Work itself. Sharing a changed version, a patch, or a Bundle is not
allowed.

The source comes with it. Whatever you share has to include the complete source,
free of charge. Sharing only a program without the source is not allowed.

No extra locks. You cannot add rules, fees, accounts, license keys, copy
protection, region limits, or any other legal or technical barrier that stops
someone from doing something this license lets them do.

It is free. You cannot charge for the Work or for access to it. You cannot add it
to anything that costs money, runs ads, or needs a subscription. You cannot put
it into a paid bundle, a paid collection, a marketplace listing, or a sponsored
download page.


4. If you let other people use it over a network

You may let other people use the unchanged Work over a network only if all of
this is true:

 1. The use is not commercial, as defined above.
 2. Every person who uses it can see this license and our credit.
 3. Every person who uses it can easily download the complete source of the exact
    version they are using, for free, from the same place they reach the
    service, with no account and no catch.

You may never let anyone use a changed version over a network. Not for free, not
for a small group, and not as a test.


5. No commercial use

You may not use the Work, or anything made from it, for commercial purposes. This
is true for every part of the Work and every use, large or small. If you think
your use might be commercial, treat it as commercial and ask for permission. We
may say yes to certain commercial uses, but only in writing, only for the use we
approve, and we can attach conditions or say no for any reason.


6. No building on the Work in public

Only section 2(c) lets you change the Work, and that is private. You may not share
a Bundle, or run one over a network, if it contains the Work or any part of it.

If you want to build something public on top of the Work, ask us first. If we say
yes, the finished project will have to be released under this license, and we may
add other conditions.


7. Things you must never do

Whatever else this license says, you may not do any of these.

 - Use the Work for AI use, or let anyone else do it.
 - Let a bot, scraper, or crawler collect the Work, unless we have said so in
   writing.
 - Take the Work apart to get at its source code, weights, keys, or prompts if
   we did not provide them, whether by decompiling, disassembling, decrypting,
   probing, or any other method.
 - Get around a limit on how the Work can be reached or used.
 - Remove, hide, or alter any notice, credit, watermark, or identifier in the
   Work.
 - Publish benchmark results, comparisons, reviews, or security findings about
   the Work without our written permission. Reporting a problem to us privately
   is always fine and welcome (see section 12).
 - Use the names "Canyon Lake Labs", "Koine OS", or "Axiom", or our logos or the
   look and feel of our products, as the name or brand of anything. You may use
   them only to give honest credit as section 3 asks.
 - Use the Work to build, train, or improve something that competes with the
   Work or with our other products.
 - Use the Work to break the law, harm people, deceive people, or violate anyone
   else's rights.


8. Who owns what

The Work is licensed to you. It is not sold to you. We keep all ownership of the
Work, including copyright, trademarks, and any patents, and we keep every right
we have not clearly given to you.

Nothing in this license gives you any right by accident or by implication. Selling
you a copy, tolerating something you do, or staying quiet about it does not give
you extra permission.

If you make a changed version, we own whatever rights you would otherwise have in
the parts that come from the Work, to the fullest extent the law allows. If you
send us ideas, suggestions, or feedback, you give us a permanent, worldwide, free
license to use them any way we like, with no credit and no payment.

If you sue anyone, claiming the Work infringes a patent, every permission in this
license ends for you the moment you file.

Some parts of the Work may belong to other people and come with their own
license. This license does not change those terms and does not give you any
rights in that material.


9. What happens if you break the rules

If you break any term of this license, your permission to use the Work ends
automatically. No notice from us is needed.

If it was your first violation and you fix it fully within 30 days of finding out
about it, your permission comes back on its own. In any other case, it comes back
only if we say so in writing.

When your permission ends, you must stop using the Work, delete every copy and
changed version you have (including backups), and if we ask, confirm in writing
that you did.

People who received a copy from you while you were following the rules keep their
own permission, directly from us, for as long as they follow the rules too.

We may stop offering the Work whenever we want, and we may release future
versions under different terms. A version you got while following these terms
stays under these terms, as long as you keep following them.


10. Remedies

If you break this license, we may suffer harm that money cannot fully repair. You
agree that we can ask a court to order you to stop, without having to post a
bond, on top of every other remedy the law gives us. That can include
collecting the profits you made from the violation, plus our reasonable legal
fees and costs.


11. No promises, and limits on what we owe

The Work is provided as it is. We make no promises about it. We do not promise it
works, is safe, is accurate, is secure, suits your purpose, or does not infringe
someone else's rights, and we disclaim every warranty the law lets us disclaim.

To the fullest extent the law allows, we are not responsible for any loss or
damage that comes from the Work or from this license, whether direct or indirect,
and including lost data, lost income, or any other loss, even if we were warned it
could happen. If a court decides we owe you something anyway, the most we owe in
total is zero dollars (US$0).

Some places do not allow these limits. Where that is the case, they apply only as
far as the law allows. Other rights you may have, such as rights of privacy,
publicity, or moral rights, may also limit how you can use the Work. This license
may not give you every permission your project needs.


12. Reporting a security problem

If you find a vulnerability, please tell us privately at support@canyonlakelabs.com. Give us
a reasonable amount of time to fix it before you tell anyone else. Sending a
report does not give you any extra rights under this license.


13. Limits of this license

You do not have to follow this license for parts of the Work that are in the
public domain, or when the law lets you use the Work without permission, such as
under fair use or fair dealing. Nothing here takes those rights away from you.


14. The legal fine print

Whole agreement. This license is everything we have agreed about the Work. It
replaces anything said or written earlier.

If part of it fails. If a court finds some part unenforceable, that part is
reduced as little as needed, and everything else stays in force.

If we do not enforce. If we do not insist on a term, or are slow to, that does not
mean we have given it up.

Which rule wins. If another notice about the Work contradicts this license, the
stricter one applies.

Nobody else can change this license. Only we can edit, replace, or sublicense the
terms that apply to the Work. We may offer the Work to others under different
terms if we choose. That does not change your terms.

Who can give permission. Permission to do something this license does not allow
is valid only if it comes from us, in writing. Nobody else can grant it for us.

Questions and permission requests: support@canyonlakelabs.com


